          "**Urinary incontinence (UI)** is the complaint of **any involuntary loss of urine**; it affects about **25-45% of adult women** (15-30% in Indian community studies), a third of people over 65 and over half of nursing-home residents. [EAU 2025]",
          "The classification examiners expect is by **type** (table below): **stress, urgency, mixed, overflow, functional and continuous** - because type decides first-line treatment. [EAU 2025]",
